  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2b0d28dc1905fe4478aee2c13c77d063, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The docks. Import and logistics, as the permit says. Now I am going home. Stamp it.
    midDaysAnswer: One of my warehouses. I am moving certain goods somewhere safer. Six districts is a lot of property to watch.
    finalDaysAnswer: My shelter under the old grain exchange. I went to count what is left. The count was short. Don't make my evening worse.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: The tram depot. I drive the number four line. Honest work, officer. Nothing more.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: My brother's apartment in Leningrad. I only moved here last week. Nothing in this city is mine yet.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: My flat. One room, rented. I have never owned property, officer. I am a simple man.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  - question: Are you experiencing any symptoms?
    earlyDaysAnswer: I don't get sick. Never have. Men who get sick don't last long in my line of work.
    midDaysAnswer: A cough. Dock air, officer, not whatever you are writing down. Choose your next word carefully.
    finalDaysAnswer: I don't discuss my health with a man holding a stamp. I am standing. That is all you need to know.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: A weak chest, since childhood. The polyclinic sees me every week. I am used to it.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: No cough. I have never set foot on the docks. The air down there is poison.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Nothing. I am a young man, officer. Twenty-five. The body heals itself.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - Smart uniform. I hope there is a smart man wearing it.
    - Take your time, officer. I am a patient man. Ask anyone who works for me.
    - You have a family, I assume. Hold onto that.
    midDays:
    - The city is reorganizing. Smart people are already choosing sides.
    - I own three blocks that used to belong to the state. Funny how that works out.
    - You are still at your post. Good. That means you are useful.
    finalDays:
    - When the dust settles, I will still be here. Will you?
    - Stamp the paper, officer. We both know who actually runs this gate.
    - I control what is left. That is not a threat. It is simply a fact.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
